.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt LIBTZFSD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzfsd_connect ,
.Nm tzfsd_request ,
.Nm tzfsd_release ,
.Nm tzfsd_ping ,
.Nm tzfsd_mount_dir
.Nd client interface to the tzfsd storage daemon
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libtzfsd
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In tzfsd.h
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_connect "void"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_request "int chan" "const struct tzfsd_req *req" "struct tzfsd_grant *out"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_release "int chan" "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_ping "int chan"
.Ft int
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir "int handle_fd" "int rdonly"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm libtzfsd
is the client library for
.Xr tzfsd 8 ,
the
.Sy [TZFS]
storage daemon.
A consumer asks
.Xr tzfsd 8
for storage of a given lifetime and receives a rights-limited
TrustedZFS dataset handle, which it then drives with the
.Xr trustedzfs 3
verb interface.
This library only
.Em obtains
the handle; it does not duplicate the verb surface.
Its symbols use the
.Sy tzfsd_
prefix so a program may link both this library and
.Xr trustedzfs 3
without collision.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_connect
connects the well-known daemon socket
.Pa /var/run/tzfsd.sock
and returns a channel descriptor, or -1 with
.Va errno
set.
A sandboxed caller handed a pre-connected channel at bootstrap skips this and
passes that descriptor as
.Fa chan
to the calls below.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_request
asks for a handle described by
.Fa req :
.Bl -tag -width ".Va lifetime" -offset indent
.It Va name
logical claim name within the requesting bundle.
.It Va rights
the
.Dv ZH_*
mask to grant; the returned handle carries no more than these.
.It Va lifetime
.Dv TZFSD_PERSISTENT
or
.Dv TZFSD_EPHEMERAL .
.El
.Pp
On success it returns 0 and fills
.Fa out ,
whose
.Va handle_fd
the caller owns and must
.Xr close 2 ,
and whose
.Va dataset
holds the resolved dataset name for audit.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_release
destroys the ephemeral claim previously granted under
.Fa name .
It is idempotent: a missing claim is success.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_ping
verifies the daemon is answering.
.Pp
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir
mounts a granted handle and returns a directory descriptor for its root,
selecting a read-only mount when
.Fa rdonly
is nonzero.
It is a thin wrapper over
.Xr tzfs_mount 3
and requires the handle to carry
.Dv ZH_MOUNT .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn tzfsd_connect
and
.Fn tzfsd_mount_dir
return a descriptor, or -1 with
.Va errno
set.
The remaining functions return 0 on success or -1 with
.Va errno
set to the daemon-reported error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr trustedzfs 3 ,
.Xr tzfsctl 8 ,
.Xr tzfsd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
